-- #3676 (undetermined goal with zero impls of its declaration accepted).
-- `roundtrip`'s body leaves the goal `Sz ?a` pinned by neither argument nor
-- result. Its interface is `zi3676_mb.Sz`, and no impl of that declaration
-- exists anywhere in the program: the one `impl Sz Widget` belongs to
-- `zi3676_ma`'s same-spelled `Sz`, a different interface. With no candidate,
-- nothing can discharge the goal, so every verb owes `T-NO-IMPL` naming
-- `lib.zi3676_mb.Sz` (DICT-SEMANTICS OD3, zero arm). Accepting it lets the
-- same-spelled impl answer for the wrong interface.
import lib.zi3676_ma.{Widget(..)}
import lib.zi3676_mb.{roundtrip}

main = println (roundtrip 14)
